 as (Number of 1’s in range [1,i — 1]) + (Number of 0’s in range [i + 1, n]). There are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") queries so this solution takes "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/d4ce9f007b0f74842e6bd60512e52d7840c4cdd0e67d011a3efc38f7b18993a7.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" time."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The problem was written by abacadaea."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/7036"}